## 1. Gorgias AI Agent

{% logo src="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/devanshug2307/agentskills-blog-content/main/images/best-ai-agents-for-post-purchase-2026/logos/gorgias-ai-agent.png" name="Gorgias AI Agent" size=40 /%}

**What it is.** The AI layer of the Gorgias ecommerce helpdesk. For this topic, the important part is its Actions feature: prebuilt templates that let the agent change a Shopify order instead of only describing the policy.

**Who it is for.** Shopify brands that already run support in Gorgias, or are willing to move there.

**Documented post-purchase actions** (Gorgias docs page "AI Agent Actions: make changes to Shopify orders", read November 25, 2026):

- **Cancel order:** checks that the order is `unfulfilled`, cancels it, restocks the product, refunds the full amount paid and sends a confirmation email.
- **Edit shipping address:** checks that the order is unfulfilled, asks the shopper to confirm the new address, then updates it in Shopify.
- **Remove order item:** confirms the item with the shopper, removes and restocks it, refunds the amount of the removed item and emails the updated order.
- **Replace order item:** swaps one item for another after a stock check. If the total goes down it refunds the difference. If the total goes up, it hands the ticket to your team.
- **Reship order for free:** duplicates a previous order when the agent judges a package lost in transit or the shopper reports damage.
- **Add to order note:** writes a note such as "address updated by AI Agent" so humans can audit the change.

**Pros**

- The action list is concrete and public, including the preconditions.
- Every change step has a built-in shopper confirmation or a human handover, for example when payment increases.
- Setup is template-based: AI Agent, Actions, See all templates, pick Shopify, Create and Enable.

**Cons**

- Cancel and address edits only change Shopify. Gorgias says the change is not passed to 3PL or fulfillment apps, and points to separate Actions for ShipStation, ShipMonk and ShipBob.
- The replace action handles one item out, one item in. Two or more items go to a human.
- Address edits cannot recalculate tax or shipping, so the agent will not refund or charge the difference.

**Benefits for post-purchase.** The minutes right after checkout are when most cancel and address requests arrive, and a human may be offline. Gorgias frames the 24/7 availability for exactly that window.

**Pricing (as of November 25, 2026).** Gorgias sells the helpdesk and the AI Agent separately.

| Helpdesk plan | Price | Tickets included |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Starter | $10 per month, monthly billing only | 50 |
| Basic | $50 per month billed annually, $60 monthly | 300 |
| Pro | $300 billed annually, $360 monthly | 2,000 |
| Advanced | $750 billed annually, $900 monthly | 5,000 |
| Enterprise | Custom quote | Over 5,000 conversations a month |

AI Agent interactions are priced at $0.90 each on annual plans or $1.00 on monthly plans, and each one also counts as a helpdesk ticket, according to the pricing FAQ. The page's structured data adds that overage above a plan's included automated interactions is billed at $1.50 per interaction, so the effective rate depends on how many interactions your plan already includes. Confirm your rate with sales. Included automated interactions run from 30 on Starter and Basic to 190 on Pro and 530 on Advanced.

**Free tier or trial.** We confirmed no free plan. Starter is the cheapest entry at $10 per month.

**Standout use case.** A 2,000-ticket Shopify store that wants "cancel within two hours, otherwise route to a human" without writing code.

**Skip it if** your fulfillment starts within minutes and you cannot add a 3PL cancel step, or your store is not on Shopify.

