## 2. Intercom Fin

{% logo src="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/devanshug2307/agentskills-blog-content/main/images/best-ai-agents-for-post-purchase-2026/logos/intercom-fin.png" name="Intercom Fin" size=40 /%}

**What it is.** Intercom's AI agent. For ecommerce, Intercom ships "Fin for Ecommerce" with Procedures (multi-step workflows) and a library of Shopify data connector templates that read and change orders.

**Who it is for.** Shopify merchants that use Intercom, and larger teams that want Fin on top of another helpdesk such as Salesforce (Intercom's pricing FAQ says that works).

**Documented post-purchase actions** (Intercom Help articles read November 25, 2026):

- **Look-ups:** order status, items, shipping address and tracking, payment transactions, refunds already issued, order timeline (up to 50 events per order), gift card balance and discount code validity.
- **Quote a refund first:** Calculate Shopify Refund and Calculate Shopify Shipping Refund return what a refund would be without moving money. The quote is order-level and shipping-level, not per line item, and the currency must match the order exactly.
- **Change an order:** Cancel Shopify Order and Update Shopify Order (note, tags, email, shipping address).
- **Refund:** Create Shopify Refund and Refund Shopify Shipping.
- **Goodwill:** Issue Shopify Gift Card, Disable Shopify Gift Card, and one-time fixed-amount or percentage discount codes.
- **Procedures:** Intercom lists where-is-my-order, returns, refunds, exchanges and order updates or cancellations as common Procedure use cases. Intercom's Fin ecommerce solutions page says Fin can verify the order, check eligibility against your policy, generate return labels, issue refunds and confirm the outcome, and escalate with context when manual approval is needed.

**Pros**

- The refund quote step lets a Procedure tell the shopper the exact amount before anything is issued.
- Identity guard: Fin returns only orders that belong to the verified customer, or to an email verified with a one-time code.
- Intercom documents the risky bits openly. Cancel, Update and Create Refund templates ship without a confirmation step, and Intercom tells you to add one in the connector description or the Procedure.

**Cons**

- Fin for Ecommerce is Shopify-only, requires Intercom, and is not sold standalone, per Intercom's own FAQ. WooCommerce, Magento, BigCommerce and custom storefronts are out.
- Gift card templates need `read_gift_cards` and `write_gift_cards` scopes that Shopify Support must grant; until then they return authorization errors.
- Preview mode does not make live data connector calls, so you must test connectors in a real conversation.

**Benefits for post-purchase.** Procedures plus templates cover the full sequence: verify the customer, check policy, quote, confirm, refund, hand off if unsure.

**Pricing (as of November 25, 2026).** Fin is priced at $0.99 per outcome, or $1.99 per outcome for Fin Voice. An outcome counts when a customer confirms the issue is resolved, does not ask for more help after Fin responds, or Fin completes a Procedure (including handoffs). Using Fin with an existing helpdesk carries no seat costs and a minimum monthly commitment (Intercom's example is 50 outcomes). Intercom's own helpdesk seats are listed at $85 per seat per month (Advanced) and $132 (Expert); the Essential plan shows $29 struck through to $19 per seat per month with a "New customers save 35%" note, so $19 appears to be the new-customer price.

**Free tier or trial.** The Essential, Advanced and Expert plans show "Start free trial" on the pricing page.

**Standout use case.** A Procedure that says: look up the order, run the refund quote, confirm the amount with the shopper, then call Create Shopify Refund, escalating if the order is already fulfilled.

**Skip it if** you are not on Shopify or you want a per-ticket price instead of per-outcome billing.

{% callout type="info" %}
A contradiction between sources: Chargeflow's November 2026 blog says Fin's order cancellations "stay with your team", while Intercom's own help center lists a Cancel Shopify Order template. The likely reconciliation is that cancellation is available as a template you must configure, not a default behavior. We did not test it.
{% /callout %}

{% figure src="https://cdn.sanity.io/images/4bgok82s/monorepo-static-assets/c6a08c512ed22b89503aaf59e7488612c102dfac-2400x1260.jpg" alt="Fin for Ecommerce page social image" caption="Fin for Ecommerce social image. Source: Intercom (fin.ai/ecommerce)." /%}

## 3. Narvar NAVI

{% logo src="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/devanshug2307/agentskills-blog-content/main/images/best-ai-agents-for-post-purchase-2026/logos/narvar-navi.png" name="Narvar NAVI" size=40 /%}

**What it is.** NAVI is the consumer-facing agent in Narvar's "agentic post-purchase" offering, powered by what Narvar calls IRIS, its identity, policy and signal layer.

**Who it is for.** Mid-market and enterprise retailers that already use Narvar for tracking and returns, and run a helpdesk such as Gladly, Kustomer, Salesforce, Zendesk or Microsoft Dynamics.

**Documented capabilities** (Narvar's agentic page, read November 25, 2026, all vendor-reported):

- Answers where-is-my-order questions with a tracking card (status, live map, actions) on the retailer site, in-app, or inside agentic assistants.
- Delivery issue resolution: evaluates a missing-package claim, approves it if eligible, and orchestrates replacement actions across the helpdesks listed above.
- Proactive exchanges: when a shopper says an item does not fit, it checks inventory in real time and offers an exchange.
- Fraud and abuse controls: a "Unified Policy Control" layer applies return, claim and service policies across channels, and NAVI communicates a trust score.
- Admin recommendations: IRIS suggests policy changes, such as enabling proactive exchanges, with projected outcomes.

The page says NAVI can "approve or deny claims, check inventory, apply retailer policies, and trigger downstream workflows inside existing systems."

**Pros**

- Policy-first design: retailers set return, claim and risk rules and the agent enforces them across channels, including in-store and call center.
- Sits above the helpdesk, so it does not require replacing it.
- Exchange-first logic aims at keeping revenue instead of refunding.

**Cons**

- No public pricing, no public action reference and no independent results that we could find. Narvar's page spells MCP as "Modern Content Protocol", which is not the standard expansion (Model Context Protocol). We treat the page's MCP claims as unverified.
- Narvar's own NAVI product page URL that we guessed returned 404. Everything here comes from the agentic page.

**Benefits for post-purchase.** If your pain is WISMO volume and "lost package" claims at scale, Narvar's pitch targets exactly that, with policy control rather than free-form generation.

**Pricing.** Not published (as of November 25, 2026). Contact sales.

**Free tier or trial.** None found.

**Standout use case.** Auto-approving a lost-package claim that meets policy, then triggering a replacement in the retailer's existing helpdesk.

**Skip it if** you are a small Shopify store that wants to see a price and a doc page before talking to anyone.

{% figure src="https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/67925857df43acae16e8d057/69617fb571c46669179406cf_Agentic_Meta-Image.png" alt="Narvar agentic post-purchase page social image" caption="Narvar agentic post-purchase page image. Source: Narvar (corp.narvar.com/agentic-ai-post-purchase)." /%}

## 4. AfterShip (agent and Post-purchase MCP)

{% logo src="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/devanshug2307/agentskills-blog-content/main/images/best-ai-agents-for-post-purchase-2026/logos/aftership.png" name="AfterShip" size=40 /%}

**What it is.** AfterShip sells tracking, returns and shipping products. It now also runs an MCP server for post-purchase data, and its pricing page lists AI features by plan.

**Who it is for.** Brands that use AfterShip Tracking or Returns and want an operator to ask Claude, Cursor or ChatGPT things like "show me exception shipments from the last 7 days".

**The MCP server** (AfterShip docs, read November 25, 2026):

- Server URL: `https://mcp.aftership.com/post-purchase`. Transport: Streamable HTTP only; SSE and stdio are not supported.
- 21 tools: 9 read your data, 12 change it.
- Tracking: search shipments, open a checkpoint timeline, edit shipment details, retrack a stalled shipment, or mark one delivered, lost or returned to sender.
- Returns: search returns, open an RMA, approve it, record received items with a grade, resolve it, comment, and manage allowlist and blocklist rules.
- Writes confirm first: the agent shows the record, field and old and new values and waits for approval. It must not invent a value, and it must not promise that a refund has landed if the tool did not say so.
- The agent can do only what your AfterShip role allows, and tools need an active plan for the product they touch.

**Pros**

- The write rules are specific and conservative.
- The workflow maps the real RMA lifecycle: approve, receive, resolve, and it cannot skip steps.
- Plan tiers are public with a volume table.

**Cons**

- This is an operator tool, not a shopper-facing refund agent.
- Some writes cannot be undone through the server: no undo for an approved return, no reopening a resolved or rejected return, no reversing a manually marked shipment status.
- The shopper-facing agent features (exception handling, Order Edits for shoppers) sit on the Premium Tracking tier, and we did not find an action reference for them.

**Benefits for post-purchase.** One conversation can find the stalled parcel, retrack it, and tell you which returns are waiting on approval, without opening three admin screens.

**Pricing (as of November 25, 2026, from AfterShip's pricing page).**

| Product and plan | Price | Included volume |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Tracking Essentials | $49 per month annual, $59 monthly | 1,000 shipments |
| Tracking Premium | $99 per month annual, $118 monthly | 1,000 shipments |
| Returns Essentials | $205 per month annual, $245 monthly | 500 returns |
| Returns Premium | $420 per month annual, $499 monthly | 500 returns |
| Shipping Essentials | $39 per month | 1,000 shipments |
| Enterprise | Custom | Above 5,000 per month |

Usage above the quota is billed as overage at 1.3x the unit price. Tracking Premium adds "AI agent for exception handling", AI delivery date estimates and Order Edits for shoppers. Essentials plans include an "AI Agent for setup and Q&A".

**Free tier or trial.** The pricing page says "Start with a free trial."

**Standout use case.** A weekly clean-up prompt for expired and exception shipments, with the agent proposing retracks you approve one by one.

**Skip it if** you want an agent that talks to shoppers and issues refunds on its own.

```json
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "aftership-post-purchase": {
      "command": "npx",
      "args": ["mcp-remote", "https://mcp.aftership.com/post-purchase"]
    }
  }
}
```

*The snippet above is our adaptation of the `mcp-remote` bridge pattern that Loop documents for Claude Desktop, pointed at AfterShip's published URL. We did not test it. Follow AfterShip's own client setup steps for your client.*

## 5. Loop Returns

{% logo src="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/devanshug2307/agentskills-blog-content/main/images/best-ai-agents-for-post-purchase-2026/logos/loop-returns.png" name="Loop Returns" size=40 /%}

**What it is.** A returns and exchanges platform for Shopify brands, now with a hosted MCP server.

**Who it is for.** Brands that want exchanges and store credit to win over refunds, and ops teams who want to query returns through an AI client.

**The MCP server** (Loop docs, read November 25, 2026):

- Endpoint: `https://api.loopreturns.com/mcp`, with authentication negotiated through OAuth discovery.
- Clients listed as supported without extra setup: Claude (desktop and web), Cursor, VS Code Copilot, ChatGPT, Perplexity and Microsoft Copilot Studio.
- Read tools documented: `list-returns-tool`, `get-return-tool` and `get-return-timeline-tool`. You can filter by status, label status, outcome (refund, credit, exchange and combinations), a fraud-risk flag and warranty returns.
- Role-based permissions: the MCP server enforces the same roles as the Loop Admin.
- Rate limits: 600 tool calls per hour per authenticated user.

**Pros**

- Clear permission model and rate limits are published.
- Outcome filters (exchange, credit, refund) match how returns teams actually triage.
- Loop is listed in the Claude connector directory, so setup is a few clicks.

**Cons**

- The documentation page we read covers read-only tools. We did not confirm any MCP tool that approves, processes or refunds a return. The return detail card shows buttons for Process, Cancel, Close, Reject and Timeline, but that is an interface element, not a documented write tool.
- No shopper-facing AI agent is part of what we read.

**Benefits for post-purchase.** Ask which returns are flagged for review, which delivered returns have not been processed, or what happened on one return, in plain language.

**Pricing (as of November 25, 2026).** The Returns plan is $340 per month and includes up to 1,000 returns annually, Shop Now, Instant Exchange, Bonus Credit and fraud prevention. A Checkout+ tier is free software plus return shipping, but "not every merchant qualifies"; eligibility depends on order and return volume.

**Free tier or trial.** Checkout+ is free for eligible merchants. No trial was listed.

**Standout use case.** A Monday prompt: "List returns delivered in the last 7 days that haven't been processed yet."

**Skip it if** you need an agent that writes refunds through MCP today, or you are not on Shopify.

