## 6. Sierra

{% logo src="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/devanshug2307/agentskills-blog-content/main/images/best-ai-agents-for-post-purchase-2026/logos/sierra.png" name="Sierra" size=40 /%}

**What it is.** An enterprise AI agent platform. Sierra's homepage says you can deploy a single agent across chat, SMS, WhatsApp, email, voice and ChatGPT, and that pricing is outcome-based ("you only pay for the value Sierra delivers").

**Who it is for.** Large consumer brands with engineering and CX operations teams, and the budget for a custom deployment.

**What we could verify.** The homepage, its channel list and its outcome-based pricing statement. We did not find a public list of post-purchase actions, a pricing sheet or a docs page describing refund, exchange or address-change tools. Anything Sierra does in a Shopify or OMS integration is therefore set up per customer and is not something we can document.

**Pros**

- Outcome-based pricing aligns cost with a resolved conversation instead of a seat.
- One agent definition across many channels, including ChatGPT.
- The homepage says a single agent deploys across chat, SMS, WhatsApp, email, voice and ChatGPT, which can reduce per-channel duplication of policy logic (our inference, untested).

**Cons**

- No public price and no public action reference.
- A platform, not a template library: expect integration work for every post-purchase action.

**Benefits for post-purchase.** If you already know you need voice and messaging for a large catalog and order volume, a platform vendor can build the refund, exchange and tracking flows against your own systems.

**Pricing.** Outcome-based; no public numbers as of November 25, 2026. Contact sales.

**Free tier or trial.** None listed.

**Standout use case.** One agent handling the same order-status question over SMS, WhatsApp and voice with one set of rules.

**Skip it if** you are a small or mid-size Shopify store, or you want to read an action list before a sales call.

