## 7. Decagon

{% logo src="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/devanshug2307/agentskills-blog-content/main/images/best-ai-agents-for-post-purchase-2026/logos/decagon.png" name="Decagon" size=40 /%}

**What it is.** A customer support AI agent platform built around Agent Operating Procedures (AOPs): workflows written in natural language that define what the agent should do, with testing, observability and an analytics suite around them. It covers chat, voice and email in one intelligence layer.

**Who it is for.** Support and CX operations teams at mid-market and enterprise companies that want to own workflow logic without engineering sprints.

**What we could verify.** Decagon's homepage describes AOPs, the three channels and a results panel with figures such as 70% chat and voice resolution, 80% deflection and $1M revenue from fully AI-handled conversations. These are vendor-reported marketing figures from unnamed customers and we did not verify any of them. We did not find a post-purchase action reference or public pricing page (our guessed pricing URL returned 404).

**Pros**

- AOPs let non-engineers edit refund, return and exchange logic in plain language.
- One layer for voice, chat and email.
- Testing and observability are part of the pitch, which matters when an agent is allowed to move money.

**Cons**

- No public pricing and no public per-action documentation.
- The homepage metrics are unattributed and cannot be reproduced.

**Benefits for post-purchase.** Return and refund policies are exactly the kind of branching business rules AOPs are designed to express. Whether Decagon ships prebuilt Shopify, Loop or AfterShip connectors is something to ask for in a demo.

**Pricing.** Not published as of November 25, 2026.

**Free tier or trial.** None listed.

**Standout use case.** Encoding "refund if within 30 days and item not final sale, otherwise offer store credit" in a procedure that a support lead can edit.

**Skip it if** you want transparent self-serve pricing, or want prebuilt Shopify action templates you can read about in advance.

