## 8. Zendesk AI agents

{% logo src="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/devanshug2307/agentskills-blog-content/main/images/best-ai-agents-for-post-purchase-2026/logos/zendesk-ai-agents.png" name="Zendesk AI agents" size=40 /%}

**What it is.** The AI agents built into Zendesk's Support and Suite plans. For post-purchase work, the relevant feature is actions: Zendesk documents four types: configured actions, API integrations, action flows and custom actions.

**Who it is for.** Teams already on Zendesk who want an agent that can read and write to Shopify, a returns portal or an OMS through APIs they configure.

**How actions work** (Zendesk help article "About actions in AI agents", read November 25, 2026):

- **Custom actions** let the agent call an API you specify to fetch or change data outside Zendesk. Zendesk recommends them for new integrations; older integration-builder API integrations remain available.
- **Action flows** are multi-step sequences that perform actions in Zendesk and external systems, for integrations that need several calls.
- **Configured actions** update session parameters, add labels or send conversation details to a CRM.
- Branching in an action flow leaves the agent with only Success and Fallback scenarios, so you pass a parameter at the end of the flow to tell it what to do next.

Zendesk's pricing page also lists an AI agent builder that creates agents from natural-language procedure descriptions, 80+ languages and "Integrations and actions" on every Suite plan. We did not find prebuilt, documented "cancel order" or "issue refund" templates; you build the integration yourself.

**Pros**

- AI agents are included in every Suite and Support plan. Billing is per automated resolution, which Zendesk defines as a request resolved by the AI agent without escalation to a human.
- Custom actions work with any REST API, so Shopify, Loop and AfterShip are reachable with effort.
- Narvar's page names Zendesk as one of the helpdesks it orchestrates replacement actions across, so it combines with a specialist.

**Cons**

- Build-your-own: no ready-made refund action to point to.
- Action flow outputs cannot be tested in the dialogue builder, per Zendesk's article.

**Benefits for post-purchase.** If your support operation already runs on Zendesk, you avoid a platform migration and can wire a refund call into your own policy checks.

**Pricing (as of November 25, 2026, Zendesk pricing page).**

| Plan | Annual, per agent per month | Monthly, per agent per month | Included automated resolutions |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Support Team | $19 | $25 | 5 per agent per month |
| Suite Team | $55 | $69 | 5 per agent per month |
| Suite Professional | $115 | $149 | 10 per agent per month |

Extra resolutions cost $1.50 each on a committed volume or $2.00 each pay-as-you-go. Copilot (the agent-assist add-on) is listed at $50 per agent per month billed annually. Voice AI agents require Zendesk voice, and the QA product is an add-on.

**Free tier or trial.** A 14-day trial with access to Suite Professional features, per the pricing FAQ.

**Standout use case.** A custom action that calls your returns portal's API, wrapped in a condition that keeps refunds above a threshold on a human queue.

**Skip it if** you are not on Zendesk, or you want prebuilt Shopify order actions without building them.

## 9. Siena AI

{% logo src="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/devanshug2307/agentskills-blog-content/main/images/best-ai-agents-for-post-purchase-2026/logos/siena-ai.png" name="Siena AI" size=40 /%}

**What it is.** An AI customer service agent aimed at ecommerce brands. Siena's homepage says it handles everything from "where's my order?" to "I want to start my return", including updating addresses, generating labels, issuing refunds and sending replacements in a single flow.

**Who it is for.** DTC brands that want an agent from a vendor focused on ecommerce, and are fine paying a platform fee.

**What we could verify.** The pricing page and a sample chat on the homepage in which the agent applies a missed discount code and refunds the difference. These are marketing statements; we did not find a docs page that lists each action or the order systems it connects to.

**Pros**

- Pricing is public and simple: a platform fee plus a per-ticket automation price.
- An unlimited sandbox is included in the platform fee, so you can test before routing real tickets.
- Broad claimed action coverage in one flow: addresses, labels, refunds, replacements.

**Cons**

- The $750 per month platform fee is a floor that smaller stores may not clear.
- No public action documentation and no independently verifiable results; the homepage quote of "50% of conversations at 90%+ CSAT" is one customer's statement.

**Benefits for post-purchase.** If the homepage claims hold in your store, one agent covers tracking, returns, address changes and replacements without stitching vendors together.

**Pricing (as of November 25, 2026).** A platform fee of $750 per month for the core AI engine and unlimited sandbox, an Automation Pack at $0.90 per automated ticket, and a support and implementation package (onboarding plus Slack support) with no price shown.

**Free tier or trial.** The sandbox is unlimited, but no free plan or trial was listed.

**Standout use case.** A "forgot my discount code" refund-the-difference flow, which is the example Siena itself shows.

**Skip it if** your volume is too low to justify $750 a month, or you need documented action-level controls before signing.

## 10. Chargeflow

{% logo src="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/devanshug2307/agentskills-blog-content/main/images/best-ai-agents-for-post-purchase-2026/logos/chargeflow.png" name="Chargeflow" size=40 /%}

**What it is.** A chargeback and dispute platform for ecommerce. It is the odd one out on this list: it does not take refund requests from shoppers. It handles what happens when a refund, a cancel or an address change did not satisfy the customer and a dispute arrives.

**Who it is for.** Merchants whose AI agents (or humans) refund, cancel and re-ship at volume, and who want a downstream safety net.

**What it does** (Chargeflow pricing page and its November 12, 2026 blog post, read November 25, 2026, vendor material):

- **Insights:** analytics across stores and processors, repeat-disputer flags, weekly summaries.
- **Prevent:** scores transactions post-checkout and before fulfillment so you can auto-approve, verify or cancel risky orders.
- **Alerts:** real-time chargeback alerts matched to a transaction and refunded automatically, with credit claims filed for duplicate or invalid alerts.
- **Automation:** AI-built evidence and submission for disputes, with a 4x ROI guarantee on pay-for-performance pricing.

**Pros**

- Pay-for-performance on recovery: no fee until a chargeback is recovered.
- A free analytics tier with no credit card.
- The blog's guardrails (cap AI-triggered refunds, check for open disputes first, log every agent action against the order) are practical for anyone deploying an action agent.

**Cons**

- It does not answer shoppers, so it complements rather than replaces the others.
- The headline claims (up to 90% fraud reduction, up to 98% lower dispute rate, a 4x ROI guarantee) are vendor-reported.
- The comparison blog it wrote about this topic ranks its own product on the list, which is a conflict of interest we have accounted for by cross-checking each competitor claim against that competitor's own docs.

**Benefits for post-purchase.** After an agent refunds, a dispute can still be filed on the same order. Chargeflow's Alerts product is designed to intercept those before they become formal chargebacks.

**Pricing (as of November 25, 2026).**

| Product | Price |
| --- | --- |
| Insights | $0, free forever |
| Prevent | $0.10 per scanned transaction; first 1,000 free |
| Alerts | $29 per alert, fully handled |
| Automation | 25% of each recovered chargeback; no payment until recovery |

The 25% fee does not include the dispute fee. Chargeflow also advertises up to 70% off for eligible startups.

**Free tier or trial.** Insights is free forever, and the first 1,000 Prevent scans are free.

**Standout use case.** Refund agents cause some disputes by refunding too late. Alerts are meant to catch the pre-dispute notice and refund before the formal chargeback.

**Skip it if** your dispute volume is negligible, or you are looking for a shopper-facing agent.

