A worked example, using only the published numbers. Suppose 500 shopper requests a month are fully resolved by the agent, and your helpdesk is already paid for. On Intercom's published rate that is 500 x $0.99 = $495. On Siena's published terms it is $750 + (500 x $0.90) = $1,200. On Zendesk's pay-as-you-go rate it is 500 x $2.00 = $1,000, before any included resolutions are subtracted. These are list-price arithmetic only. They ignore what each vendor counts as an outcome, a resolution or an automated ticket, and those definitions differ, so treat the comparison as an order of magnitude and not as a quote.

