## Head-to-head: the three closest pairs

### Gorgias AI Agent vs Intercom Fin: which to pick

Both act on Shopify orders, but they package it differently.

| | Gorgias AI Agent | Intercom Fin |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Action style | Prebuilt actions (cancel, edit address, remove, replace, reship, note) | Data connector templates plus Procedures |
| Refund control | Refunds as a side effect of other actions | Quote first (Calculate Shopify Refund), then Create Shopify Refund |
| Safety defaults | Unfulfilled check; confirmation steps in the action | Verified-identity lookup; add your own confirmation to write templates |
| Platform coupling | Gorgias helpdesk | Intercom, or Fin on another helpdesk |
| Platforms | Shopify | Shopify only for Fin for Ecommerce |
| Pricing | Per AI interaction plus helpdesk tickets | Per outcome ($0.99) |

**Pick Gorgias** if you want a ready list of actions with the preconditions already written, and your support lives in Gorgias. **Pick Fin** if you want a quote-then-refund sequence and are willing to add confirmation steps yourself. Both need a test conversation before you trust them.

### Narvar NAVI vs AfterShip: which to pick

| | Narvar NAVI | AfterShip |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Who it serves | Shoppers, through the retailer's channels | Operators, through an AI client over MCP |
| Documented depth | Marketing page only | Docs with a 21-tool reference |
| Writes | Claim approvals and exchange offers (claimed) | 12 write tools, each behind a confirmation |
| Price visibility | Contact sales | Public tiers |

**Pick Narvar** if you are a larger retailer who wants a policy engine across channels and will negotiate. **Pick AfterShip** if you want something you can read, price and try this week.

### Loop Returns vs AfterShip Returns: which to pick

Both sell returns software with AI-client access. Loop's documented MCP surface that we could confirm is read-only (list, detail, timeline) with outcome filters. AfterShip documents approve, receive and resolve as write tools with a confirmation rule and an irreversible-actions warning. If you want an assistant that moves a return through its lifecycle, AfterShip's documentation is further along. If you want a polished read-and-triage view with strict role-based permissions and a published rate limit, Loop's is clearer. Entry prices are close: Loop Returns $340 per month versus AfterShip Returns Essentials $205 per month on annual billing (500 returns a month), though plan contents differ.

